 ],
 "notes": "The music room added to an existing house above the Rio de la Plata, the river taken as south. From the entrance elevation (gravel forecourt, low exposed-concrete podium with a broad step, a glazed wall between board-formed concrete wall ends, a carved screen beside it, the dark metal roof slab with a wood soffit overhanging all round, a small flue on top), the river-side views (deep roof over a covered terrace held by a single column, a concrete block at the west end standing past the roof, frameless glass, grey boulders along the podium's edge, tall native grass in drifts on a dry lawn) and the glazed corridor view (a glass link with a thin dark roof, glass both sides, running to the existing house). This pass: the native grass is drygrass tufts in drifts along the river side instead of green blobs; the lavender north of the forecourt is low grey-green mounds in rows (no lavender colour in the palette, 'plant' stands in); the link's roof is thin and dark, not white; the existing house's glass volume gets a dark fascia; more and larger boulders along the podium; the west end block is carried up to the roof's underside as the photographs show; a flue on the roof. Still guessed: the room's exact plan and depth (scaled from ~3 m glazing and a person), the existing house beyond the link (a dark-framed glass volume and a pale rendered block), the tree positions. From above the dark roof covers most of the room, as it does in life."
